\ A word body the runtime image carries as bytecode names the `inline` words expansion erased, the
\ way an interpreted or a compiled one does.
\
\ Reaching `outer` by name at run time is what puts it on the tier this test exists for. Every word
\ the freeze discovers has to compile, and a compiled body bakes its rows at codegen; only a word
\ nothing calls statically is left running the bytecode the image decoded. `>quotation` builds that
\ call out of a string, so the freeze never sees it.
\
\ The `outer` row itself is absent from the chain because the quotation `>quotation` builds calls it
\ in tail position. That is ordinary tail-call behaviour and predates this test.

use "fixtures/aot_inline_error_frames_image_caller.1z" ;

stdout 42 "outer" >quotation call drop
